ADDENDA <Act No. 18542, Dec. 7, 2021>
Article 1 (Enforcement date)
This Act shall enter into force 6 months after the date of its promulgation; provided, Articles 2 through 4 of the Addenda shall enter into force on the date of its promulgation.
Article 2 (Preparation for establishment)
(1) The Minister of the Interior and Safety shall establish a National Trauma Recovery Center Establishment Committee (hereinafter referred to as "Establishment Committee") in charge of business affairs regarding the establishment of the Center and business affairs regarding the appointment of directors and auditors as at the time of establishment within 3 months from the date of promulgation of this Act.
(2) The Establishment Committee shall be comprised of up to 7 incorporators commissioned by the Minister of the Interior and Safety, and the Vice Minister of the Interior and Safety shall serve as the chairperson of the Establishment Committee.
(3) The Establishment Committee shall prepare the articles of incorporation of the Center, affix his or her name and seal or sign it, and obtain authorization therefor from the Minister of the Interior and Safety.
(4) Upon obtaining authorization pursuant to paragraph (3), the Establishment Committee shall, without delay, complete the registration of the establishment of the Center with joint signatures.
(5) The president of the Center at the time of its establishment shall be appointed by the Minister of the Interior and Safety.
(6) The Establishment Committee shall, when the president of the Center is appointed by the president, transfer its business affairs to the president without delay.
(7) The Establishment Committee shall be deemed dissolved when the transfer of business affairs under paragraph (6) is completed, and its members shall be deemed dismissed.
Article 3 (Establishment expenses)
Expenses incurred in establishing the Center shall be borne by the State.
Article 4 (Special cases concerning preparation of budgetary documents)
Budgetary documents of the Center for the first business year that commences after the establishment of the Center may be prepared by the Establishment Committee.

